-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 27: LODGMENT IN COURT, MONEY IN REGISTRY AND PAYMENT TO SHERIFF (rules 1 to 21), layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc6-order-23.l4.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a definition that "means", a condition introduced by "if", "where",
--                "unless" or "only if", a flat negative ("must not be computed", "no interest is payable"), a threshold in the
--                text's own figures ("less than $30,000"), or a time fixed in the text's own words and missed.
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent on what follows a failure to comply with a "must", a list is
--                not closed ("includes"), a fact lives in another Order (Order 9 Rule 17, Order 14, Order 33), or a grant
--                ("may") is limited by its own wording and the case is outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every requirement here is subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise (O 3 r 2(1)).
-- "order" in this Order means an order or judgment of a Court, whether made in Court or in chambers (Rule 1): a function here that
-- mentions "an order" uses that meaning.  A period is counted by Order 3, Rule 3 (roc1's range).
-- The answers of Order 9 Rule 17, Order 14 and Order 33 (roc2 and roc7's ranges) come in as the inputs `o 9 r 17 ...`, `o 14 ...` and `o 33 ...`.

