-- src:4110 | 2. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), any trustee wishing to make a payment into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act must apply by summons supported by an affidavit setting out — ( a )
-- src:4111 | a short description of the trust and of the instrument creating it or (as the case may be) of the circumstances in which the trust arose;
-- src:4112 | ( b )
-- src:4113 | the names of the persons interested in or entitled to the money or securities to be paid into Court with their addresses so far as known to the trustee;
-- src:4114 | ( c )
-- src:4115 | the trustee’s submission to answer all such inquiries relating to the application of such money or securities as the Court may make or direct; and
-- src:4116 | ( d )
-- src:4117 | an address where the trustee may be served with any summons or order, or notice of any proceedings, relating to the money or securities paid into Court.
@ref O 27 r 2(1) (src:4110-4117)
GIVEN `the trustee wishes to make a payment into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trustee applied by summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit describes the trust and the instrument creating it, or the circumstances in which the trust arose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit names the persons interested in or entitled to the money or securities, with their addresses so far as known to the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the trustee's submission to answer all inquiries relating to the application of the money or securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit gives an address where the trustee may be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 2(1) the trustee has applied by summons supported by an affidavit as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the trustee wishes to make a payment into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any trustee wishing to make a payment into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act"
        IF (NOT `the trustee applied by summons`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the trustee "must apply by summons" and does not say what follows if the trustee does not
        IF `paragraph (2) applies` THEN JUST TRUE -- the affidavit is not required: see paragraph (2)
        IF `the summons is supported by an affidavit` AND `the affidavit describes the trust and the instrument creating it, or the circumstances in which the trust arose` AND `the affidavit names the persons interested in or entitled to the money or securities, with their addresses so far as known to the trustee` AND `the affidavit states the trustee's submission to answer all inquiries relating to the application of the money or securities` AND `the affidavit gives an address where the trustee may be served` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the summons must be "supported by an affidavit setting out" (a) to (d) and does not say what follows if it is not

