        IF `o 27 r 2(2) paragraph (2) says no affidavit need be filed under paragraph (1)` `the money or securities represent a legacy, or residue or any share of a legacy` `a minor or a person resident outside Singapore is absolutely entitled to it` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (2)": paragraph (2) says "no affidavit need be filed under paragraph (1)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "must apply by summons supported by an affidavit setting out" (a) to (d)
