§§ `Rule 5 -- Crediting lodgment and dividends`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 27 r 5 what was received` IS ONE OF
    `o 27 r 5(a) principal money`
    `o 27 r 5(b) dividends`
    `o 27 r 5 something else`

-- src:4129 | 5. Any principal money or dividends received by the Accountant‑General in respect of securities in Court must be placed in his or her books — ( a )
-- src:4130 | in the case of principal money — to the credit to which the securities whereon such money were standing at the time of the receipt of the money; and
-- src:4131 | ( b )
-- src:4132 | in the case of dividends — to the credit to which the securities whereon such dividends were accrued were standing at the time of closing of the transfer books of such securities previously to the dividends becoming due.
@ref O 27 r 5 (src:4129-4132)
GIVEN received IS A `o 27 r 5 what was received`
      `the credit to which the securities were standing at the time of the receipt of the principal money` IS A STRING
      `the credit to which the securities were standing at the time of the closing of the transfer books previously to the dividends becoming due` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`o 27 r 5 the credit to which the Accountant-General places the amount in his or her books` MEANS
    CONSIDER received
    WHEN `o 27 r 5(a) principal money` THEN JUST `the credit to which the securities were standing at the time of the receipt of the principal money`
    WHEN `o 27 r 5(b) dividends` THEN JUST `the credit to which the securities were standing at the time of the closing of the transfer books previously to the dividends becoming due`
    WHEN `o 27 r 5 something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any principal money or dividends received by the Accountant‑General in respect of securities in Court"

