        IF `the rate is fixed by the Minister for Finance` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says "at such rate as is from time to time fixed by the Minister for Finance" and does not say what follows if the rate is fixed otherwise

-- src:4138 | (2) Such money is deemed not to be placed on deposit when the amount is reduced below $30,000.
@ref O 27 r 6(2) (src:4138)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 6(2) the money is deemed not to be placed on deposit` MEANS
    IF amount LESS THAN `o 27 r 6 the deposit threshold`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "when the amount is reduced below $30,000"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- Computation of interest`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4140 | 7. —(1) Interest upon money on deposit must not be computed on a fraction of $1. (2) Interest upon money on deposit accrues by calendar months, and must not be computed by any less period.
@ref O 27 r 7(1) (src:4140)
GIVEN `the amount on which the interest is computed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 7(1) interest on money on deposit may be computed on the amount` MEANS
    IF FLOOR `the amount on which the interest is computed` EQUALS `the amount on which the interest is computed`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says interest "must not be computed on a fraction of $1" and does not say that it is computed on a whole amount
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Interest upon money on deposit must not be computed on a fraction of $1"

DECLARE `o 27 r 7(2) period` IS ONE OF
    `o 27 r 7(2) a calendar month`
    `o 27 r 7(2) a period less than a calendar month`
    `o 27 r 7(2) a period longer than a calendar month`

@ref O 27 r 7(2) (src:4140)
GIVEN period IS A `o 27 r 7(2) period`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 7(2) interest on money on deposit is computed by the period` MEANS
    CONSIDER period
    WHEN `o 27 r 7(2) a calendar month` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 27 r 7(2) a period less than a calendar month` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be computed by any less period"
    WHEN `o 27 r 7(2) a period longer than a calendar month` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says interest "accrues by calendar months" and bars a shorter period and does not speak of a longer one

-- src:4141 | (3) Such interest begins on the first day of the calendar month next succeeding that in which the money is placed on deposit, and ceases from the last day of the calendar month next preceding the day of the withdrawal of the money from deposit.
@ref O 27 r 7(3) (src:4141)
GIVEN `the day the money is placed on deposit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 27 r 7(3) the first day on which interest begins` MEANS
    Month (Date ((Day (Month `the day the money is placed on deposit`)) PLUS 32))

-- Fork F-O27-1: "ceases from the last day of the calendar month next preceding the day of the withdrawal" can mean that interest
-- is no longer earned for that last day (taken here: the function answers that day, as the day FROM which interest ceases) or that
-- interest runs through that last day and ceases the day after.  "Begins on the first day of the calendar month next succeeding" has
-- no such doubt: interest begins on that day.
@ref O 27 r 7(3) (src:4141)
GIVEN `the day the money is withdrawn from deposit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 27 r 7(3) the day from which interest ceases` MEANS
    Date ((Day (Month `the day the money is withdrawn from deposit`)) MINUS 1)

`o 27 r 7(4) fifteen days after the end of the year` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 15
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:4142 | (4) Interest which has accrued for or during the year ending on 31 December in every year, on money then on deposit must, on or before 15 days thereafter following, be placed by the Accountant‑General to the credit to which such money is standing.
@ref O 27 r 7(4) (src:4142)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`o 27 r 7(4) the day the 15 days run from` MEANS
    Date 31 12 year

@ref O 27 r 7(4) (src:4142)
GIVEN `the day the Accountant-General placed the interest to the credit` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 7(4) the interest for the year is placed to the credit on or before 15 days after the year ends` MEANS
    IF `the day the Accountant-General placed the interest to the credit` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "on or before 15 days thereafter following"

-- src:4143 | (5) When money on deposit is withdrawn from deposit, the interest on the money which has accrued and has not been credited must be placed to the credit to which the money is then standing.
@ref O 27 r 7(5) (src:4143)
GIVEN `the money on deposit is withdrawn from deposit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest accrued and not credited is placed to the credit to which the money is then standing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 7(5) the interest accrued and not credited is placed to the credit to which the money is then standing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the money on deposit is withdrawn from deposit`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "When money on deposit is withdrawn from deposit"
        IF `the interest accrued and not credited is placed to the credit to which the money is then standing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the interest "must be placed to the credit" and does not say what follows if it is not

-- src:4144 | (6) When money on deposit consists of sums which have been placed on deposit at different times, and an order is made dealing with the money, and part of such money has to be withdrawn from deposit for the purpose of executing such order, the part or parts of the money dealt with by such order last placed and remaining on deposit at the time of such withdrawal must, for the purpose of computing interest, be treated as so withdrawn unless the order otherwise directs.
@ref O 27 r 7(6) (src:4144)
GIVEN `the money on deposit consists of sums placed on deposit at different times` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made dealing with the money and part of it has to be withdrawn to execute the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part is the part or parts dealt with by the order last placed and remaining on deposit at the time of the withdrawal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 7(6) the part is treated as withdrawn for the purpose of computing interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the money on deposit consists of sums placed on deposit at different times`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "When money on deposit consists of sums which have been placed on deposit at different times"
        IF (NOT `an order is made dealing with the money and part of it has to be withdrawn to execute the order`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "and an order is made dealing with the money, and part of such money has to be withdrawn from deposit for the purpose of executing such order"
        IF `the order otherwise directs` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the order otherwise directs"
        IF `the part is the part or parts dealt with by the order last placed and remaining on deposit at the time of the withdrawal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph treats "the part or parts ... last placed and remaining on deposit" as withdrawn

-- src:4145 | (7) Unless otherwise directed by an order, interest credited on money on deposit must, when or so soon as it amounts to or exceeds $30,000, be placed on deposit and, for the purpose of computing interest upon it, must be treated as having been placed on deposit on the last yearly day on which any such interest became due.
@ref O 27 r 7(7) (src:4145)
GIVEN `the amount of the interest credited` IS A NUMBER
      `an order directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 7(7) the interest credited is placed on deposit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order directs otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless otherwise directed by an order"
        IF `the amount of the interest credited` AT LEAST `o 27 r 6 the deposit threshold` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "when or so soon as it amounts to or exceeds $30,000"

@ref O 27 r 7(7) (src:4145)
GIVEN `the last yearly day on which any such interest became due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 27 r 7(7) the day the interest is treated as placed on deposit` MEANS
    `the last yearly day on which any such interest became due`

