§§ `Rule 9 -- Name of payee to be stated in order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4149 | 9. —(1) Every order which directs funds in Court to be paid, transferred, or delivered out must state in full the name of every person to whom such payment, transfer or delivery is to be made, unless the name is to be stated in a certificate of the Registrar. (2) In the case of payment to a firm, it is sufficient to state the business name of such firm.
@ref O 27 r 9(1) (src:4149)
GIVEN `the order directs funds in Court to be paid, transferred or delivered out` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order states in full the name of every person to whom the payment, transfer or delivery is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name is to be stated in a certificate of the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 9(1) the order states the name of every payee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the order directs funds in Court to be paid, transferred or delivered out`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every order which directs funds in Court to be paid, transferred, or delivered out"
        IF `the order states in full the name of every person to whom the payment, transfer or delivery is to be made` OR `the name is to be stated in a certificate of the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the order "must state" the name and does not say what follows if it does not

@ref O 27 r 9(2) (src:4149)
GIVEN `the payment is to a firm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order states the business name of the firm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 9(2) it is sufficient for the order to state the business name of the firm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the payment is to a firm`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "In the case of" read as "where": assumed, see F-ASSUMED): "In the case of payment to a firm, it is sufficient to state the business name of such firm"
        IF `the order states the business name of the firm` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "it is sufficient to state the business name" says what is enough and does not say that anything else is not

DECLARE `o 27 r 9(3) to whom the money is paid` IS ONE OF
    `o 27 r 9(3) any one or more of the co-partners`
    `o 27 r 9(3) the survivor of them`
    `o 27 r 9(3) someone else`

-- src:4150 | (3) When money in Court is by an order directed to be paid to any persons described in the order, or in a certificate of the Registrar, as co‑partners, such money may be paid to any one or more of such co‑partners, or to the survivor of them.
@ref O 27 r 9(3) (src:4150)
GIVEN `the order or the certificate of the Registrar describes the persons as co-partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      payee IS A `o 27 r 9(3) to whom the money is paid`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 9(3) the money may be paid to the payee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the order or the certificate of the Registrar describes the persons as co-partners`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any persons described in the order, or in a certificate of the Registrar, as co‑partners"
        IF payee EQUALS `o 27 r 9(3) any one or more of the co-partners` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF payee EQUALS `o 27 r 9(3) the survivor of them` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the money "may be paid to any one or more of such co‑partners, or to the survivor of them"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 10 -- Payment out on death of payee`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4152 | 10. —(1) When funds in Court are by an order directed to be paid, transferred, or delivered to any person named or described in an order, or in a certificate of the Registrar, the funds, or any portion of the funds for the time being remaining unpaid, untransferred, or undelivered, may, unless the order otherwise directs, on proof of the death of that person, whether — ( a )
-- src:4153 | on or after the date of such order; or
-- src:4154 | ( b )
-- src:4155 | in the case of payment directed to be made to a creditor as such, before the date of such order,
-- src:4156 | be paid, transferred or delivered to the legal personal representatives of the deceased person, or to the survivor or survivors of them.
@ref O 27 r 10(1) (src:4152-4156)
GIVEN `an order directs funds in Court to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person named or described in the order or in a certificate of the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is proof of the death of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the death was on or after the date of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment was directed to be made to a creditor as such and the death was before the date of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 10(1) the funds may be paid, transferred or delivered to the legal personal representatives of the deceased person or to the survivor or survivors of them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an order directs funds in Court to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person named or described in the order or in a certificate of the Registrar`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "When funds in Court are by an order directed to be paid, transferred, or delivered to any person named or described in an order, or in a certificate of the Registrar"
        IF `the order otherwise directs` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the order otherwise directs"
        IF (NOT `there is proof of the death of that person`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "on proof of the death of that person" ("on proof" read as "upon")
        IF `there is proof of the death of that person` AND (`the death was on or after the date of the order` OR `the payment was directed to be made to a creditor as such and the death was before the date of the order`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on proof of the death of that person, whether (a) on or after the date of such order; or (b) in the case of payment directed to be made to a creditor as such, before the date of such order"

-- src:4157 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply to an order directing funds in Court to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person expressed, in the order or certificate of the Registrar, to be entitled to such funds — ( a )
-- src:4158 | as trustee, executor or administrator; or
-- src:4159 | ( b )
-- src:4160 | otherwise than in his or her own right, or for his or her own use.
@ref O 27 r 10(2) (src:4157-4160)
GIVEN `the order directs funds to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person expressed to be entitled as trustee, executor or administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order directs funds to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person expressed to be entitled otherwise than in his or her own right, or for his or her own use` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 10(2) paragraph (1) applies to the order` MEANS
    IF `the order directs funds to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person expressed to be entitled as trustee, executor or administrator` OR `the order directs funds to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person expressed to be entitled otherwise than in his or her own right, or for his or her own use`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (1) does not apply to an order directing funds in Court to be paid, transferred or delivered to a person expressed, in the order or certificate of the Registrar, to be entitled to such funds — (a) as trustee, executor or administrator; or (b) otherwise than in his or her own right, or for his or her own use"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2) takes out two kinds of order and says nothing of when paragraph (1) applies

DECLARE `o 27 r 10(3) relation to the deceased` IS ONE OF
    `o 27 r 10(3) widower`
    `o 27 r 10(3) widow`
    `o 27 r 10(3) child`
    `o 27 r 10(3) father`
    `o 27 r 10(3) mother`
    `o 27 r 10(3) brother`
    `o 27 r 10(3) sister`
    `o 27 r 10(3) some other relation`

`o 27 r 10(3) the asset ceiling` MEANS 10000

`o 27 r 10(3) the form of the declaration` MEANS "Form 46"

-- src:4161 | (3) If no administration has been taken out to the estate of such deceased person who has died intestate, and whose assets do not exceed the value of $10,000, including the amount of the funds directed to be so paid, transferred or delivered to him or her, such funds may be paid, transferred, or delivered to the person who, being widower, widow, child, father, mother, brother or sister of the deceased, would be entitled to take administration to his or her estate, upon a declaration by such person in accordance with Form 46.
@ref O 27 r 10(3) (src:4161)
GIVEN `no administration has been taken out to the estate of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased died intestate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assets of the deceased, including the amount of the funds` IS A NUMBER
      relation IS A `o 27 r 10(3) relation to the deceased`
      `that person would be entitled to take administration to the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 10(3) the funds may be paid, transferred or delivered to the person upon a declaration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `no administration has been taken out to the estate of the deceased`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no administration has been taken out to the estate of such deceased person"
        IF (NOT `the deceased died intestate`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who has died intestate"
        IF `the assets of the deceased, including the amount of the funds` GREATER THAN `o 27 r 10(3) the asset ceiling` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whose assets do not exceed the value of $10,000, including the amount of the funds"
        IF relation EQUALS `o 27 r 10(3) some other relation` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person who, being widower, widow, child, father, mother, brother or sister of the deceased, would be entitled to take administration"
        IF (NOT `that person would be entitled to take administration to the estate`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the person who, being widower, ..., would be entitled to take administration to his or her estate" is a relative clause that names the person, with no "only"
        IF form EQUALS `o 27 r 10(3) the form of the declaration` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "upon" read as "where"): "upon a declaration by such person in accordance with Form 46"

-- src:4162 | (4) When funds in Court are by an order directed to be paid, transferred, or delivered to any persons as legal personal representatives, such funds, or any portion of the funds for the time being remaining unpaid, untransferred, or undelivered, may, upon proof of the death of any such representatives, whether on or after the date of such order, be paid, transferred or delivered to the survivor or survivors of them.
