        IF `there is proof of the death of one of them` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "upon" read as "where"): "upon proof of the death of any such representatives"

