      `o 14 the money is paid into Court under Order 14` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `o 33 the money is paid into Court under Order 33` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the money is paid into Court as security for costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investment is in securities in which trustees are by law permitted to invest trust money in their hands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 11(3) the Court may direct that the money in Court be invested in trustee securities` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 27 r 6(1)(a) the money is paid into Court under Order 9, Rule 17, Order 14 or Order 33, or as security for costs` `o 9 r 17 the money is paid into Court under Order 9, Rule 17` `o 14 the money is paid into Court under Order 14` `o 33 the money is paid into Court under Order 33` `the money is paid into Court as security for costs`
    WHEN JUST excepted THEN
        IF excepted
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for "any money in Court, other than money under Order 9, Rule 17, Order 14 or Order 33, or as security for costs"; paragraph (4) deals with Order 33 money
        ELSE
            IF `the investment is in securities in which trustees are by law permitted to invest trust money in their hands`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be invested in any of the securities in which trustees are by law permitted to invest trust money in their hands"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the money is paid under Order 9 Rule 17, Order 14 or Order 33 is not known

`o 27 r 11(4) the amount the money must exceed` MEANS 250000

