`o 27 r 11(4) the Court may direct that the money in Court be placed on deposit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the money at the time of the making of the order` AT MOST `o 27 r 11(4) the amount the money must exceed` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only if at the time of the making of the order, it exceeds the sum of $250,000"
        IF `o 33 the money is paid into Court under Order 33` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the money is under Order 33 is in another part's range
        IF `o 33 the money is paid into Court under Order 33` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is about "money in Court under Order 33"
        IF `the deposit is with a bank or finance company in Singapore to earn interest` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "placed on deposit with any bank or finance company in Singapore to earn interest"

-- src:4168 | (5) Any application for an order under paragraph (4) must be served on the Sheriff.
@ref O 27 r 11(5) (src:4168)
GIVEN `the application is for an order under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application was served on the Sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 11(5) the application was served on the Sheriff` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is for an order under paragraph (4)`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any application for an order under paragraph (4)"
        IF `the application was served on the Sheriff` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the application "must be served on the Sheriff" and does not say what follows if it is not

