§§ `Rules 12 to 14 -- Certificate, publication of list and unclaimed funds`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4170 | 12. The Accountant‑General, upon a request signed by or on behalf of a person claiming to be interested in any funds in Court standing to the credit of an account specified in such request, must, unless there is good reason for refusing, issue a certificate of the amount and description of such funds.
@ref O 27 r 12 (src:4170)
GIVEN `the request is signed by or on behalf of a person claiming to be interested in funds in Court standing to the credit of an account specified in the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is good reason for refusing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 12 the Accountant-General must issue a certificate of the amount and description of the funds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the request is signed by or on behalf of a person claiming to be interested in funds in Court standing to the credit of an account specified in the request`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "upon a request signed by or on behalf of a person claiming to be interested in any funds in Court standing to the credit of an account specified in such request"
        IF `there is good reason for refusing` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless there is good reason for refusing"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4172 | 13. In the month of January in every year, the Accountant‑General must cause to be published in the Gazette a list of accounts not dealt with for a period of 4 years or more and must give the title and number of the cause or matter and the title of the ledger credit in which funds are outstanding, and the balance of the funds in each account.
@ref O 27 r 13 (src:4172)
GIVEN `the date the list is published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 13 the list is published in the Gazette in the month of January` MEANS
    IF (Month `the date the list is published in the Gazette`) EQUALS (Year `the date the list is published in the Gazette`)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the first day of its month is the first day of its year, so it is in January
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "In the month of January in every year"

@ref O 27 r 13 (src:4172)
`o 27 r 13 the number of years` MEANS 4

GIVEN `the years since the account was last dealt with` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 13 the account is one the list must include` MEANS
    IF `the years since the account was last dealt with` AT LEAST `o 27 r 13 the number of years`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a list of accounts not dealt with for a period of 4 years or more" is a scope limit with no "only", so the Rule does not say that other accounts are left off

@ref O 27 r 13 (src:4172)
GIVEN `the list gives the title and number of the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list gives the title of the ledger credit in which funds are outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list gives the balance of the funds in each account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 13 the list gives what the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the list gives the title and number of the cause or matter` AND `the list gives the title of the ledger credit in which funds are outstanding` AND `the list gives the balance of the funds in each account`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says the Accountant-General "must give" these and does not say what follows if he or she does not

-- The core `Time unit` has no years, so the six years and the four years are plain numbers of years (see NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- Fork F-O27-2: rule 13 ("a list of accounts not dealt with for a period of 4 years or more") and rule 14(1) ("for a period of 6 years
-- and upwards ... must be transferred") use the same kind of threshold, and I could not tell whether it is a scope limit with no "only"
-- (ruling (c): outside it, NOTHING) or a period the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a): outside it, JUST FALSE).  Taken: rule 13
-- describes which accounts a list covers and does not say a younger account must be left off, so (c); rule 14(1) says when a duty to
-- transfer arises, so (a).  Reading rule 14(1) as (c) would answer NOTHING below 6 years; reading rule 13 as (a) would answer JUST FALSE
-- below 4 years.
`o 27 r 14(1) the number of years` MEANS 6

-- src:4174 | 14. —(1) The funds in Court or in the Sheriff’s account appearing from the books and accounts to have been in the custody of the Accountant‑General or the Sheriff for a period of 6 years and upwards, without any claim having been made and allowed thereto during that period, must be transferred and paid to the Government for the general purposes of the State. (2) If any claim is made to any part of the funds in Court or in the Sheriff’s account which are transferred and paid to the Government under paragraph (1), and if such claim is established to the satisfaction of the Court, the Government must pay to the claimant the amount of the principal so transferred and paid as aforesaid, or so much of the amount of the principal as appears to be due to the claimant.
@ref O 27 r 14(1) (src:4174)
GIVEN `the years the funds appear to have been in the custody of the Accountant-General or the Sheriff` IS A NUMBER
      `a claim was made to the funds and allowed during that period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 14(1) the funds must be transferred and paid to the Government for the general purposes of the State` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the years the funds appear to have been in the custody of the Accountant-General or the Sheriff` LESS THAN `o 27 r 14(1) the number of years` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "for a period of 6 years and upwards"
        IF `a claim was made to the funds and allowed during that period` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without any claim having been made and allowed thereto during that period"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref O 27 r 14(2) (src:4174)
GIVEN `a claim is made to part of the funds that were transferred and paid to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is established to the satisfaction of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal so transferred and paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the principal that appears to be due to the claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 27 r 14(2) the amount the Government must pay the claimant` MEANS
    IF `a claim is made to part of the funds that were transferred and paid to the Government` AND `the claim is established to the satisfaction of the Court`
    THEN
        IF `the amount of the principal that appears to be due to the claimant` GREATER THAN `the principal so transferred and paid`
        THEN `the principal so transferred and paid`
        ELSE `the amount of the principal that appears to be due to the claimant`
    ELSE 0 -- the Government must pay nothing under this paragraph unless a claim is made and established: "if such claim is established to the satisfaction of the Court"

@ref O 27 r 14(2) (src:4174)
GIVEN `a claim is made to part of the funds that were transferred and paid to the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is established to the satisfaction of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 14(2) the Government must pay the claimant` MEANS
    IF `a claim is made to part of the funds that were transferred and paid to the Government` AND `the claim is established to the satisfaction of the Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any claim is made ..., and if such claim is established to the satisfaction of the Court, the Government must pay": the number function above cannot carry a no, so this is its yes/no twin (the Rule gives the principal only, and no interest)
-- src:4175 | (3) Nothing in this Rule authorises the transfer of any funds in Court or in the Sheriff’s account standing to the separate credit of a minor, or held in a minor’s account pending the coming of age of such minor, until such minor comes of age or dies.
@ref O 27 r 14(3) (src:4175)
GIVEN `the funds stand to the separate credit of a minor, or are held in a minor's account pending the coming of age of the minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minor has come of age or died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 14(3) this Rule authorises the transfer of the funds` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the funds stand to the separate credit of a minor, or are held in a minor's account pending the coming of age of the minor` AND (NOT `the minor has come of age or died`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Rule authorises the transfer of any funds in Court or in the Sheriff's account standing to the separate credit of a minor ... until such minor comes of age or dies"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph bars a transfer of a minor's funds until the minor comes of age or dies and does not say what paragraph (1) does about other funds, or about a minor's funds after that

-- Ruling (d) of 2026-11-05: a bar "until X" is asked as its own question, "is the transfer barred yet", JUST TRUE before X and JUST FALSE after
-- X; the function above is the question "does this Rule authorise the transfer", which the bar answers JUST FALSE before X and never answers
-- yes on the bar's strength alone.
@ref O 27 r 14(3) (src:4175)
GIVEN `the funds stand to the separate credit of a minor, or are held in a minor's account pending the coming of age of the minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minor has come of age or died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 14(3) the transfer of the minor's funds under this Rule is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the funds stand to the separate credit of a minor, or are held in a minor's account pending the coming of age of the minor`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on "any funds ... standing to the separate credit of a minor, or held in a minor's account", and the paragraph does not speak of other funds
        IF `the minor has come of age or died` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): "until such minor comes of age or dies": the bar has ended
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- the bar is in force: "Nothing in this Rule authorises the transfer ... until such minor comes of age or dies"
