-- src:4177 | 15. —(1) The Sheriff must keep an account of all sums of money paid to or deposited with him or her and of all sums of money paid out by him or her. (2) All money paid to or deposited with the Sheriff must be kept in a bank or with the Accountant‑General.
@ref O 27 r 15(1) (src:4177)
GIVEN `the Sheriff keeps an account of all sums of money paid to or deposited with him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the account shows all sums of money paid out by him or her` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 15(1) the Sheriff keeps an account of all sums of money paid to, deposited with and paid out by him or her` MEANS
    IF `the Sheriff keeps an account of all sums of money paid to or deposited with him or her` AND `the account shows all sums of money paid out by him or her`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the Sheriff "must keep an account" and does not say what follows if he or she does not

DECLARE `o 27 r 15(2) where the money is kept` IS ONE OF
    `o 27 r 15(2) in a bank`
    `o 27 r 15(2) with the Accountant-General`
    `o 27 r 15(2) somewhere else`

@ref O 27 r 15(2) (src:4177)
GIVEN place IS A `o 27 r 15(2) where the money is kept`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 15(2) the money paid to or deposited with the Sheriff is kept in the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `o 27 r 15(2) in a bank` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 27 r 15(2) with the Accountant-General` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 27 r 15(2) somewhere else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the money "must be kept in a bank or with the Accountant‑General" and does not say what follows if it is kept elsewhere

-- src:4178 | (3) No interest is payable in respect of any money paid to or deposited with the Sheriff.
