      `the Registry officer receiving the money acknowledged it with a receipt of the payment or deposit given upon the payment or deposit being made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 27 r 16 the Registry officer has acknowledged the money with a receipt` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the money was paid to or deposited with the Sheriff under these Rules or a judgment or order of a Court`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Money paid to or deposited with the Sheriff under these Rules or a judgment or order of a Court"
        IF `the Registry officer receiving the money acknowledged it with a receipt of the payment or deposit given upon the payment or deposit being made` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule says the money "must be acknowledged" and does not say what follows if it is not

-- src:4182 | 17. When any payment is made under a judgment or order, the person making the payment must — ( a )
