-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The duties of Order 27 as regulative rules`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each rule says the same thing as the decision function named beside it; the decision functions are asserted
-- and the traces are run (a #TRACE prints a result and counts as no assertion on this binary).

DECLARE `o 27 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 27 the person who lodged money or securities in Court`
    `o 27 the Accountant-General`
    `o 27 the person making a payment under a judgment or order`

DECLARE `o 27 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 27 r 3 give notice of the lodgment`
    `o 27 r 7(4) place the interest for the year to the credit`
    `o 27 r 17 produce a copy of the judgment or order and give notice to the person entitled`

-- src:4120 | 3. Any person who has lodged money or securities in Court must forthwith give notice of the lodgment to every person appearing to be entitled to, or have an interest in, the money or securities lodged.
@ref O 27 r 3 (src:4120)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 27 party` `o 27 act`
`o 27 r 3 the person who lodged must give notice of the lodgment` MEANS
    PARTY `o 27 the person who lodged money or securities in Court`
    MUST `o 27 r 3 give notice of the lodgment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person who lodged money or securities in Court did not give notice of the lodgment to every person appearing to be entitled to, or have an interest in, it"

-- src:4142 | (4) Interest which has accrued for or during the year ending on 31 December in every year, on money then on deposit must, on or before 15 days thereafter following, be placed by the Accountant‑General to the credit to which such money is standing.
@ref O 27 r 7(4) (src:4142)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 27 party` `o 27 act`
`o 27 r 7(4) the Accountant-General must place the interest for the year to the credit within 15 days` MEANS
    PARTY `o 27 the Accountant-General`
    MUST `o 27 r 7(4) place the interest for the year to the credit`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the Accountant-General did not place the interest that accrued for the year ending on 31 December to the credit within 15 days after that day"

-- src:4182 | 17. When any payment is made under a judgment or order, the person making the payment must — ( a )
-- src:4183 | produce a copy of the judgment or order; and
-- src:4184 | ( b )
-- src:4185 | give notice to the person entitled to the money.
@ref O 27 r 17 (src:4182-4185)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 27 party` `o 27 act`
`o 27 r 17 the person making the payment must produce a copy and give notice` MEANS
    PARTY `o 27 the person making a payment under a judgment or order`
    MUST `o 27 r 17 produce a copy of the judgment or order and give notice to the person entitled`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the person making a payment under a judgment or order did not produce a copy of it and give notice to the person entitled to the money"
